# Copy to `.dev.vars` in this folder (gitignored). Wrangler loads it for `npm run preview`
# and local Pages Functions (`/api/chat-messages`, `/api/mongo-ping`).
#
# Clerk Dashboard → Configure → API Keys (same application as auth.aliasist.com):
# Never commit real keys to git.
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_your_clerk_secret_key
CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_your_clerk_publishable_key
#
# Agent Dashboard. Keep the worker secrets server-only.
# ALIASIST_ADMIN_USER_IDS=user_your_clerk_user_id
# AGENT_PUSH_SECRET=the-exact-secret-set-on-the-aliasist-chat-worker
# CLEARASIST_METADATA_WORKER_URL=https://clearasist-metadata.bchooper0730.workers.dev
# CLEARASIST_ADMIN_SECRET=the-exact-secret-set-on-the-clearasist-worker
#
# Optional: upstream LLM worker base for `/api/chat` proxy (no trailing slash).
# Defaults to https://llm-chat.bchooper0730.workers.dev if omitted.
# LLM_CHAT_BASE_URL=https://llm-chat.your-worker.workers.dev
#
# RAG backend base URL — used by /api/chat to fetch grounded context.
# Defaults to https://api.aliasist.tech if omitted.
# RAG_BASE_URL=https://api.aliasist.tech
#
# Homepage AI consulting demo.
# Keep GROQ_API_KEY server-side only. PUBLIC_CHAT_ENABLED lets unsigned visitors
# try the floating AI widget with a small server-side rate limit.
# PUBLIC_CHAT_ENABLED=true
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your_groq_key
#
# Optional: GitHub token for `/api/github-pr-review`.
# Use a fine-grained token with read-only repository access to raise rate limits
# or test private repo review locally. Production should use a GitHub App
# installation token or OAuth flow instead of a broad personal token.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_your_read_only_token
#
# GitHub App automation for `/api/github/webhook`.
# Copy the App ID from the GitHub App settings page. Generate a private key and
# preserve its PEM line breaks. Use the same high-entropy webhook secret in the
# GitHub App settings and Cloudflare Pages secrets.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=123456
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=Iv23example
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=replace_with_openssl_rand_hex_32_output
#
# Entertainment page (/entertainment): trending movies/TV, games, and
# display-only sports odds. Each is optional — a tab shows a "not configured"
# message if its key is missing. Weather uses Open-Meteo, which needs no key.
# TMDB_API_KEY=your_themoviedb_v3_api_key   # themoviedb.org → Settings → API
# RAWG_API_KEY=your_rawg_api_key            # rawg.io/apidocs → sign up
# ODDS_API_KEY=your_the_odds_api_key        # the-odds-api.com → sign up (free tier is metered)
#
# Related worker templates (same keys):
#   apps/llm-chat/.dev.vars.example     — POST /api/chat JWT verification
#   apps/datasist-api/.dev.vars.example — DataSist API + admin JWTs
#   website/.dev.vars.example           — standalone Pages with website/functions
